ollow in the footsteps of over 250,000 emigrants who traveled to the gold fields and rich farmlands of California during the 1840s and 1850s: the greatest mass migration in American history. The California National Historic Trail is over 5,000 miles long and covers portions of 10 states. Step into history along more than 1,000 miles of ruts and traces from travelers and their overland wagons.",fullDescription:"California National Historic Trail is an official National Park Service site. Follow in the footsteps of over 250,000 emigrants who traveled to the gold fields and rich farmlands of California during the 1840s and 1850s: the greatest mass migration in American history. The California National Historic Trail is over 5,000 miles long and covers portions of 10 states. Step into history along more than 1,000 miles of ruts and traces from travelers and their overland wagons. Visitors from all over come to experience and learn about its distinct natural formations and historic value.",thingsToDo:["Historical Exhibits","Guided Ranger Tours","Photography","Visitor Center Film","Educational Walks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Hike on the California Trail",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Follow in the footsteps of over 250,000 emigrants who traveled to the gold fields and rich farmlands of California during the 1840s and 1850s: the greatest mass migration in American history. There are a variety of hikin"}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"California Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for California National Historic Trail, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(505) 988-6098"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"No campgrounds are available within the historic site grounds. Campgrounds and hotel lodging are located in nearby towns.",wildlife:["Songbirds","White-tailed Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Squirrels"],bestView