ia’s indigenous cultures, Spanish colonialism, the Mexican Republic, US military expansion and the growth of San Francisco. All of this and more awaits you, so get out and find your park. Visitors from all over come to experience and learn about its distinct natural formations and historic value.",thingsToDo:["Hiking","Scenic Drives","Wildlife Viewing","Photography","Nature Trails","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Hike the Bolinas Ridge Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"1-11 Hours",description:"Admire redwood forests and expansive views of the Olema Valley on this dog-friendly, multi-use trail. This up-to-11-mile-long trail begins at either at the Bolinas Ridge Trailhead along Sir Francis Drake Boulevard or at "},{name:"Walk the Cross Marin Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"1-5 Hours",description:"The up-to-10.6-miles- roundtrip Cross Marin Trail is a relatively flat, easy trail that follows the historic North Pacific Coast Railroad right-of-way paralleling Lagunitas Creek. Pets are permitted on the Cross Marin Tr"},{name:"Explore Sutro Baths and Sutro Heights Park",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"1-3 Hours",description:"Explore the Sutro Bath Ruins and Sutro Heights Park"}],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Golden Gate Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Golden Gate National Recreation Area, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(415) 561-4900"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"Camping is permitted in designated campgrounds inside the area. Permits and advanced reservations are highly recommended.",wildlife:["Mule Deer","Bald Eagles","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Summit Viewpoint","Valley Vista Point","River Overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Californi