-the-gunnison-national-park",name:"Black Canyon of the Gunnison National Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C81655F-1DD8-B71B-0B4BCFFDB74EE723.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C8166E8-1DD8-B71B-0BDEB9A4EEEED807.jpg"],shortDescription:"Descend into the dramatic, sheer cliffs of Black Canyon, a chasm carved over millions of years by the Gunnison River, revealing some of the oldest exposed rock on Earth. This park offers unparalleled views into a gorge so deep and narrow that sunlight struggles to reach its floor.",fullDescription:"The Black Canyon of the Gunnison National Park showcases a profound geological wonder, with vertical walls plunging up to 2,700 feet. The Gunnison River's relentless erosion has exposed ancient Precambrian rock, providing a stark visual record of Earth's history. Visitors can experience dramatic overlooks, challenging wilderness trails, and stargazing opportunities in this International Dark Sky Park, offering a unique perspective on the power of natural forces.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:["Black Scenic Drive"],visitorCenter:{name:"Black Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(970) 641-2337"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Private Vehicle $30; Per Person $15 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Colorado, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Black%20Canyon%20of%20the%20Gunnison%20National%20Park",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/blca",b