lk the historic grounds, visit the Pioneer Cemetery where Nancy Hanks Lincoln is buried, and explore the museum to understand the profound impact these years had on one of America's greatest presidents. The site offers a poignant connection to the roots of American character and leadership.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Lincoln Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(812) 937-4541"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists no camping at this site.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Park Grounds and Trails are open year-round. For Memorial Visitor Center Hours see Visitor Center tab below.",address:"Indiana, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Lincoln%20Boyhood%20National%20Memorial",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/libo/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Memorial"},{id:"lewis-clark-national-historic-trail",name:"Lewis & Clark National Historic Trail",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/FA29AF56-DF2B-8692-40F8422E38FB9093.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/F1E53C07-CAC7-1E47-F3002F9102E59BA6.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/F21788EE-E877-C00C-257B0EB8AD8F49DB.jpg"],shortDescription:"The Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail winds nearly 4,900 miles through the homelands of more than 60 Tribal nations. It follows the historic outbound and inbound routes of the Lewis and Clark Expedition of 1803-1806 from Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania to the Pacific Ocean. Follow the trail to find the people, places, and stories that make up the complex legacy of the expedition.",fullDescription:"Lewis & Clark National Historic Trail is an official National Park Service site. The Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail winds nearly 4,900 miles through the homelands of more than 60 Tribal nations. It follows the historic outbound and inbound routes of the Lewis and Clark Expedition of 1803-1806 from Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania to the Pacific Ocean. Follow the trail to find the people, places, and stories that make up the complex legacy of the expedition. Visitors from all over come to experience and learn about its distinct natural formations and historic value.",thingsToDo:["Historical Exhibits","Guided Ranger Tours","Photography","Visitor Center Film","Educational Walks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"South Slough Trail",difficulty:"Difficult",length:"1-3 Hours",description:"The South Slough Trail is a three mile loop that can be accessed from the Fort to Sea Trailhead or from near the North Netul Landing that features twist and turns and steep changes in elevation among large trees and a bo"},{name:"Clay Pit Pond Trail",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"15-60 Minutes",description:"The Clay Pit Pond is a half mile loop primitive trail with access at the Fort Clatsop Visitor Center picnic area. It is a great trail for those looking for a short but dynamic hike. The trail features a vernal pond surro"},{name:"Netul River Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"20-60 Minutes",description:"Take an easy approximately 1 mile stroll along the beautiful Netul River Trail. Watch for water birds, eagles and sometimes otters! Along the way you can learn about the history of logging and commerce along the Lewis an"}]