ublic",address:"Arkansas and Kansas, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=President%20William%20Jefferson%20Clinton%20Birthplace%20Home%20National%20Historic%20Site",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/wicl/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Historic Site"},{id:"pea-ridge-national-military-park",name:"Pea Ridge National Military Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7E6346-1DD8-B71B-0B7F2E71DEF77DE8.jpg",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Commemorates one of the most pivotal Civil War battles west of the Mississippi River, a Union victory that secured Missouri for the North.",fullDescription:"Pea Ridge National Military Park preserves the battlefield where, in March 1862, a decisive Union victory halted Confederate efforts to gain control of Missouri. This large-scale battle involved approximately 26,000 soldiers over two intense days, featuring significant troop movements and a diverse mix of forces, including Native American units. Visitors can explore the preserved battlefield via an auto tour, walking trails, and interpretive exhibits that recount the strategic importance and human cost of this often-overlooked Western Theater engagement.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Williams Hollow Loop Hike",difficulty:"Strenuous",length:"45-90 Minutes",description:"Hiking at Pea Ridge National Military Park is a great way to understand the true scope of the park, both in size and meaning. It is also a wonderful opportunity to experience the quiet peace of nature in bustling Northwe"}],scenicDrives:["Pea 