 decisive siege and victory at Yorktown, Virginia. Today, visitors can explore historic taverns, campsites, and roads, discovering the incredible logistics, cooperation, and international alliance that secured American independence.",thingsToDo:["Historical Exhibits","Guided Ranger Tours","Photography","Visitor Center Film","Educational Walks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Multi-Park Loop",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Park your car and stretch your legs! Visit four different National Parks in Washington, DC and begin logging miles on seven different National Historic or National Scenic trails!"},{name:"Become a B.A.R.K. Ranger!",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Become a B.A.R.K and P.U.R.R.K Ranger at Washington-Rochambeau Revolutionary Routes National Historic Trai."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Washington-Rochambeau Revolutionary Route Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Washington-Rochambeau Revolutionary Route National Historic Trail, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(215) 597-7013"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"No campgrounds are available within the historic site grounds. Campgrounds and hotel lodging are located in nearby towns.",wildlife:["Songbirds","White-tailed Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Squirrels"],bestViewpoints:["Main Commemorative Plaza","Visitor Center Overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Maryland, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Washington-Rochambeau%20Revolutionary%20Route%20National%20Historic%20Trail",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/waro/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild and comfortable weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor contact center, primary educational exhibits, and several viewpoints are fully wheelchai