ontana along the Canadian border, is a pristine wilderness of over one million acres. Renowned as the 'Crown of the Continent,' the park features spectacular horn-shaped peaks, active glaciers, pristine alpine lakes, and dense forests home to grizzly bears, wolverines, and bighorn sheep. The park is world-famous for the engineering marvel Going-to-the-Sun Road, a scenic 50-mile mountain highway crossing Continental Divide at Logan Pass, offering dramatic panoramic vistas.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Take a Half-Day Hike in Glacier",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"3-5 Hours",description:"Glacier is a hiker’s paradise. Spend part of your day on one of these 3-5 hour hikes."},{name:"Take a Full Day Hike in Glacier",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"5-12 Hours",description:"Glacier is a hiker’s paradise. Spend your whole day in nature on one of these popular trails."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Glacier Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(406) 888-7800"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Private Vehicle $35; Per Person $20 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Montana, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Glacier%20National%20Park",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/glac",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Park"},{id:"yellowstone-national-park",name:"Yellowstone National Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/28B56C01-ABED-ED7B-FDC8E6D3FC843D09.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/28B56C01-ABED-ED7B-FDC8E6D3FC843D09.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/29EB105C-BCE3-4859-9B83F22E1091AA2F.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7D5920-1DD8-B71B-0B83F012ED802CEA.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/2A83F1F6-BA74-D152-1F43D8C6910C3897.jpg"],shortDescription:"Yellowstone National Park is located primarily in Wyoming. Please refer to Wyoming for full information and details.",fullDescription:"This entry represents the portion of Yellowstone National Park located in this state. The park is famously known and managed as a single unit. For complete itineraries, visitor centers, hiking trails, camping info, and travel guides, please select Wyoming from the browse states list.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Yellowstone River Picnic Area Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"2-3 Hours",description:"Explore local highlights."},{name:"Yellowstone Lake Overlook Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"1-3 Hours",description:"Hike to a high mountain meadow for a commanding view of the West Thumb of Yellowstone Lake and the distant Absaroka Mountains."},{name:"West Thumb Geyser Basin Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"30-60 Minutes",description:"Stroll through a geyser basin of colorful hot springs and dormant lakeshore geysers situated on the scenic shores of Yellowstone Lake."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Yellowstone National Park Visitor Information",info:"Please select Wyoming for visitor center information and contact details.",hours:"Varies",phone:"Located in Wyoming.