ss National Historic Trail",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7DBDE9-1DD8-B71B-0B1F370DE4F54140.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7DB875-1DD8-B71B-0BE5099AF762C684.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7DBC60-1DD8-B71B-0B9F79E85C441052.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/6415306F-DAAC-38F2-DDDA1EC538160855.jpg"],shortDescription:"It is hard to believe that young men once rode horses to carry mail from Missouri to California in the unprecedented time of only 10 days. This relay system along the Pony Express National Historic Trail in eight states was the most direct and practical means of east-west communications before the telegraph.",fullDescription:"Pony Express National Historic Trail is an official National Park Service site. It is hard to believe that young men once rode horses to carry mail from Missouri to California in the unprecedented time of only 10 days. This relay system along the Pony Express National Historic Trail in eight states was the most direct and practical means of east-west communications before the telegraph. Visitors from all over come to experience and learn about its distinct natural formations and historic value.",thingsToDo:["Historical Exhibits","Guided Ranger Tours","Photography","Visitor Center Film","Educational Walks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Walk on the Pony Express Trail",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"There are a variety of walking and hiking opportunities along the Pony Express Trail. In some places, you may find a modern-day hiking trail. In other places, the historic trail has been replaced by an dirt or asphalt ro"}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Pony Express Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Pony Express National Historic Trail, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(505) 988-6098"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-le