ational exhibits, and several viewpoints are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Review the official NPS website prior to travel for weather warnings and temporary trail closures.","Pack plenty of water, use sun protection, and ensure you pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Recreation Area"},{id:"lower-delaware-national-wild-and-scenic-river",name:"Lower Delaware National Wild and Scenic River",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7A403C-1DD8-B71B-0B48D4D57314EA3D.jpg",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Protects key segments of the Delaware River, the largest free-flowing river in the eastern United States, rich in history and recreation.",fullDescription:"The Lower Delaware National Wild and Scenic River protects crucial free-flowing segments of the Delaware River, the largest undammed river in the eastern United States. Spanning the border of New Jersey and Pennsylvania, the protected corridor runs past scenic cliffs, historic canal towns, active farmlands, and lush forests. It provides vital habitats for migratory fish and birds, as well as outstanding opportunities for canoeing, kayaking, boating, and hiking along the historic Delaware and Raritan Canal paths.",thingsToDo:["Hiking","Scenic Drives","Wildlife Viewing","Photography","Nature Trails","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Lower Delaware Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Lower Delaware National Wild and Scenic River, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(617) 981-0466"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"Camping is permitted in designated campgrounds inside the area. Permits and advanced reservations are highly recommended.",wildlife:["Mule Deer","Bald Eagles","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Summit 