ures once housed over 15,000 working-class immigrants from over twenty countries between 1863 and 2011. Through meticulously recreated family apartments, historic neighborhood walking tours, and dynamic digital exhibits, the site explores the real-world stories of families who struggled, thrived, and helped forge the modern fabric, laws, and culture of the United States.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Lower Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(877) 975-3786"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists no camping at this site.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Timed Entry Reservation - Location $30 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Visit the Tenement Museum virtually or in person! From neighborhood walking tours and educator-led apartment tours, to digital exhibits and virtual programs, experience the museum the way that works best for you.",address:"New york, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Lower%20East%20Side%20Tenement%20National%20Historic%20Site",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/loea",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Historic Site"},{id:"martin-van-buren-national-historic-site",name:"Martin Van Buren National Historic Site",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ee97efb1483986f4.webp",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Preserves Lindenwald, the scenic estate and retirement home of Martin Van Buren, the eighth President of the United States.",fullDescription:`Martin Van Buren National Historic Site protects "Lindenwald," the elegant 36-room Italianate mansion and working farm in Kinderhook, New York, owned by the eighth U.S. President, Martin Van Buren. After his presidency, Van Buren retired here, managing his farm and orchestrating several presidential campaigns during the tumultuous, pre-Civil War decade of the 1840s. The site offers guided tours exploring Van Buren's political genius, the history of agricultural reform, and the growing national debate over slavery and union.`,thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Martin Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(518) 764-1041"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists no camping at this site.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Park grounds are open year round from 7:00 am to sunset. Visitor facilities and guided tours of the president's home are available on a seasonal basis.",address:"New york, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Martin%20Van%20Buren%20National%20Historic%20Site",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/mava",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Historic Site"},{id:"sagamore-hill-national-historic-site",name:"Sagamore Hill National Historic Site",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/ECC1F2D7-9542-D923-D10D269AC661A004.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/ECC1F2D7-9542-D923-D10D269AC661A004.jpg"],shortDescription:'Preserves the majestic estate and "Summer White House" of Theodore Roosevelt, the 26th President of the United States.',fullDescription:`Sagamore Hill National Historic Site in Oyster Bay, Long Island, preserves the beloved 23-room Queen Anne-style home of Theodore Roosevelt. From 1902 to 1908, this sprawling estate served as his "Summer White House," hosting international peace conferences, political allies, and foreign dignitaries. The site features Roosevelt's personal library containing countless historical books and hunting trophies, the scenic wooded grounds overlooking Cold Spring Harbor, and the Old Orchard Museum exploring his family life, military campaigns, and conservation achievements.`,thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Hike Sagamore Hill's Nature Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"30-60 Minutes",description:"Take a walk in the footsteps of the Roosevelts and explore the woodlands and beach of Sagamore Hill on a 0.7 mile nature trail."},{name:"Bring Your BARK Ranger for a Walk",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"30-120 Minutes",description:"Your dog is welcome to visit Sagamore Hill with you, as long as you help them be good BARK Rangers by following four simple rules: 1) Bag your pet's waste. 2) Always keep your pet on a leash. 3) Respect Sagamore Hill's w"},{name:"Visit Eel Creek and Cold Spring Harbor",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"60-120 Minutes",description:"Sagamore Hill’s nature trail leads to scenic water views of Eel creek, a tidal salt marsh creek, and a beach on Cold Spring Harbor."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Sagamore Visi