ests and scenic crests of the Appalachian Mountains.",fullDescription:"The Appalachian National Scenic Trail is a world-renowned continuous footpath extending over 2,190 miles across fourteen eastern states. In New York, the trail covers 90 miles, winding along the rugged ridge of the Hudson Highlands, crossing the Hudson River at the Bear Mountain Bridge, and passing through beautiful state parks like Harriman and Sterling Forest. This section features dramatic rock scrambles, historic trail shelters, and scenic lookouts offering panoramic views of the Hudson Valley.",thingsToDo:["Hiking","Scenic Drives","Wildlife Viewing","Photography","Nature Trails","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Multi-Park Loop",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Park your car and stretch your legs! Visit four different National Parks in Washington, DC and begin logging miles on seven different National Historic or National Scenic trails!"}],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Appalachian Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Appalachian National Scenic Trail, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(304) 535-6278"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"Camping is permitted in designated campgrounds inside the area. Permits and advanced reservations are highly recommended.",wildlife:["Mule Deer","Bald Eagles","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Summit Viewpoint","Valley Vista Point","River Overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"New york, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Appalachian%20National%20Scenic%20Trail",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/appa/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild and comfortable weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visito