f the Chesapeake watershed.",thingsToDo:["Hiking","Scenic Drives","Wildlife Viewing","Photography","Nature Trails","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Chesapeake Bay Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Chesapeake Bay, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(410) 260-2470"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"Camping is permitted in designated campgrounds inside the area. Permits and advanced reservations are highly recommended.",wildlife:["Mule Deer","Bald Eagles","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Summit Viewpoint","Valley Vista Point","River Overlook"],entranceFees:"Check the official website for current fees.",hours:"Check the official website for current hours.",address:"New york, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Chesapeake%20Bay",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/chba/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild and comfortable weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor contact center, primary educational exhibits, and several viewpoints are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Review the official NPS website prior to travel for weather warnings and temporary trail closures.","Pack plenty of water, use sun protection, and ensure you pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Recreation Area"},{id:"lower-east-side-tenement-museum-national-historic-site",name:"Lower East Side Tenement Museum National Historic Site",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/park-lower-east-side-tenement-museum-national-historic-site-new-york.webp",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/B360E148-BF7F-1653-4BFE8FB8C05E518C.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/B360E148-BF7F-1653-4BFE8FB8C05E518C.jpg"],shortDescription:"Preserves two historic tenements that tell the diverse stories of 15,000 working-class immigrants who built New York City.",fullDescription:"The Lower East Side Tenement Museum National Historic Site, affiliated with the Tenement Museum, preserves two historic brick tenement buildings on Orchard Street in Manhattan. These structures once housed over 15,000 working-class immigrants from over twenty countries between 1863 and 2011. Through meticulously recreated family apartments, historic neighborhood walking tours, and dynamic digital exhibits, the site explores the real-world stories of families who struggled, thrived, and helped forge the modern fabric, laws, and culture of the United States.",thingsToDo:["Historical Exhibits","Guided Ranger Tours","Photography","Visitor Center Film","Educational Walks"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Lower East Side Tenement Museum Visitor Information",info:"The contact point for Lower East Side Tenement Museum National Historic Site, offering exhibits, maps, pamphlets, and helpful ranger guidance for planning your visit.",phone:"(877) 975-3786"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"No campgrounds are available within the historic site grounds. Campgrounds and hotel lodging are located in nearby towns.",wildlife:["Songbirds","White-tailed Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Squirrels"],bestViewpoints:["Main Commemorative Plaza","Visitor Center Overlook"],entranceFees:"Timed Entry Reservation - Location $30 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Visit the Tenement Museum virtually or in person! From neighborhood walking tours and educator-led apartment tours, to digital exhibits and virtual programs, experience the museum the way that works best for you.",address:"New york, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Lower%20East%20Side%20Tenement%20Museum%20National%20Historic%20Site",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/loea",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild and comf