 premier opportunities for canoeing, kayaking, fishing, hiking, and camping. Visitors can explore hundreds of miles of trails, including the Appalachian Trail, marvel at scenic waterfalls like Raymondskill Falls, visit historic agricultural villages, and enjoy the stunning scenic vistas overlooking the dramatic gap in the mountain ridge.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails","Kayaking","Swimming"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Easy Hike Along Hornbecks Creek",difficulty:"Easy",length:"See nps.gov",description:"An easy, one-mile out and back hike along the Lower Hornbecks Creek will lead visitors to a small waterfall, but the waterfall is only part of the view! "}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Delaware Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(570) 426-2452"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Herons","Bald Eagles","Osprey","River Otters"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Private Vehicle $10 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"New jersey and Pennsylvania, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Delaware%20Water%20Gap%20National%20Recreation%20AreaMiddle%20Delaware%20National%20Scenic%20River",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/dewa/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Recreation Area"},{id:"middle-delaware-national-scenic-