9CE-EDA1-98EFFD3B1E833A73.jpg"],shortDescription:"A network of trails connecting the Potomac River basin across Virginia, Maryland, Pennsylvania, and Washington, D.C.",fullDescription:"The Potomac Heritage National Scenic Trail is an expansive, multi-state network of trails that traces the historic corridors of the Potomac River basin. Spanning Pennsylvania, Maryland, Virginia, and Washington, D.C., the trail connects diverse landscapes, historic canals, and scenic river valleys. In Pennsylvania, the trail connects with the Great Allegheny Passage (GAP) and the historic Forbes Road, allowing hikers, cyclists, and history enthusiasts to follow the routes of early settlers, Native Americans, and Revolutionary-era pioneers.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Explore the Civil War Defenses of Washington Hiker-Biker Trail",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"1-5 Hours",description:"Hike or bike the 7-mile trail from Fort Stanton to Fort Mahan and take in scenery that ranges from urban greenspaces to forest ecosystems, all while recreating through a historic landscape."},{name:"Multi-Park Loop",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Park your car and stretch your legs! Visit four different National Parks in Washington, DC and begin logging miles on seven different National Historic or National Scenic trails!"},{name:"Explore the Trails at Meadowood",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"1-4 Hours",description:"Hike, Bike, and Horseback Ride at Meadowood Special Recreation Management Area."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Potomac Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(301) 739-4200"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Deer