ony, and discover how Williams' revolutionary ideas became the foundation for the First Amendment of the U.S. Constitution.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Historical Exhibits","Ranger Talks"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Roger Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(401) 521-7266"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists no camping at this site.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"We're excited to welcome you to the park! Our grounds are open from dawn to dusk, and our Visitor Center is here to greet you Thursday - Sunday, from 10:00 AM to 4:00 PM.",address:"Rhode island, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Roger%20Williams%20National%20Memorial",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/rowi/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Memorial"},{id:"washington-rochambeau-revolutionary-route-national-historic-trail",name:"Washington-Rochambeau Revolutionary Route National Historic Trail",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3049B5BE-921E-7B15-7E1E4D6BD21442AB.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/31648791-F4D9-4CA7-3CD80631C81422B7.jpg"],shortDescription:"Follows the historic 680-mile land route taken by the allied French and American armies to victory at Yorktown in 1781.",fullDescription:"The Washington-Rochamb