g the Badlands",difficulty:"Easy",length:"1-5 Hours",description:"Interested in hiking at Badlands National Park? Read about rules, official trails, and the park's open hike policy here."},{name:"Hiking Badlands Back Roads With Your Dog",difficulty:"See nps.gov",length:"See nps.gov",description:"Back country roads are a great place to escape the everyday with your pet."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Badlands Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(605) 433-5361"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Deer","Red-tailed Hawks","Songbirds","Coyotes"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck"],entranceFees:"Private Vehicle $30; Per Person $15 (per nps.gov)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"South dakota, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Badlands%20National%20Park",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/badl/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Park"},{id:"wind-cave-national-park",name:"Wind Cave National Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3DDEBDBA-0714-8856-F59E16D2DB6FCB4B.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7ACD12-1DD8-B71B-0BEF13804E4498FF.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C7ACE71-1DD8-B71B-0BBD14BFE8C0C468.jpg"],shortDescription:"One of the world's longest caves, famous for its rare, delicate calcite boxwork formations