tain biking, horse riding, and backcountry hiking, combining wilderness preservation with outstanding outdoor recreation.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails","Kayaking","Swimming","Scenic Drives","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Big Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(423) 569-9778"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs","Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Herons","Bald Eagles","Osprey","River Otters","Mule Deer","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck","Summit Viewpoint","Valley Vista Point","River Overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Kentucky and Tennessee, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Big%20South%20Fork%20National%20River%20and%20Recreation%20Area*",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/biso/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platforms/trails are fully wheelchair accessible.",travelTips:["Check the official NPS website before visiting for current weather and conditions.","Carry plenty of drinking water and pack out all trash.","Review the official NPS website prior to travel for weather warnings and temporary trail closures.","Pack plenty of water, use sun protection, and ensure you pack out all trash."],nearbyAttractions:[],designation:"National Recreation Area"},{id:"obed-wild-and-scenic-river",name:"Obed Wild and Scenic River",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3C792DFB-1DD8-B71B-0B5E8EB41685A5BB.jpg",photoGallery:[],shortDescription:"Protects a beautiful, rugged, and free-flowing river system on the Cumberland Plateau, famous for rock climbing and paddling.",fullDescription:"The Obed Wild and Scenic River protects a spectacular, rugged, free-flowing river system on the Cumberland Plateau in East Tennessee. Looking much the same today as it did when the first settlers arrived, the Obed features clear waters, steep sandstone gorges rising up to 500 feet, and pristine forests. It is highly celebrated for its world-class white-water kayaking, traditional rock climbing, deep gorges, and dark night skies, offering visitors an immersive wilderness adventure.",thingsToDo:["Sightseeing","Photography","Guided Walks","Wildlife Viewing","Hiking","Nature Trails","Kayaking","Swimming","Scenic Drives","Outdoor Exploration"],hikingTrails:[],scenicDrives:["Park Scenic Loop (12 miles)"],visitorCenter:{name:"Obed Visitor Center",info:"The main visitor contact point, providing maps, informational brochures, and educational displays.",phone:"(423) 346-6294"},rangerPrograms:["Daily Ranger-led Educational Talks","Junior Ranger Activity Programs","Daily Ranger-led Interpretive Walks","Junior Ranger Badge Activities"],campingInfo:"NPS lists camping here; see nps.gov for campgrounds and reservations.",wildlife:["Herons","Bald Eagles","Osprey","River Otters","Mule Deer","Foxes","Coyotes","Diverse Bird Species","Small Mammals"],bestViewpoints:["Main Overlook","Visitor Center Observation Deck","Summit Viewpoint","Valley Vista Point","River Overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Open 24 hours a day (per nps.gov; visitor center hours vary)",address:"Tennessee, USA",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Obed%20Wild%20and%20Scenic%20River",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/obed/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring and Autumn (mild weather)",accessibilityInfo:"The visitor center and several designated viewing platfor