Bay and the historic fort ramparts."},{name:"Engineer's Wharf Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"Short interpretive trail focusing on the history of the harbor."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Casemate Museum",info:"Serves as the main visitor center and interpretive hub.",phone:"757-788-3391",hours:"10:00 AM - 4:30 PM"},rangerPrograms:["Freedom's Fortress walking tours","Civil War history talks"],campingInfo:"No camping facilities available.",wildlife:["Osprey","Blue heron","Bottlenose dolphin","Crabs"],bestViewpoints:["Fort Ramparts","Old Point Comfort Lighthouse"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"Fort Monroe National Monument is open year-round for outdoor activities like walking and exploring the historic grounds. Residents occupy many of the buildings.",address:"495 Fenwick Rd, Fort Monroe, VA 23651",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Fort+Monroe+National+Monument",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/fomr/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring through early autumn",accessibilityInfo:"Most of the historic area is flat and accessible; museum is ADA compliant.",travelTips:["Bring sun protection for the seawall","Visit the lighthouse for photos","Check for road closures as it is a mixed-use community"],nearbyAttractions:["Virginia Air and Space Science Center","Yorktown Battlefield"],designation:"National Monument"},{id:"george-washington-birthplace-national-monument",name:"George Washington Birthplace National Monument",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3D13D699-B89E-E495-18D9F3D4826FD0BE.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/3D13D699-B89E-E495-18D9F3D4826FD0BE.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/B1E849B2-E9A9-D53F-76496DE9CEC6C806.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/B1BC42A4-B749-0E55-A6D101DCD7ABBE57.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/91339E64-D121-5059-DAC9A369214DCD5A.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/914DDB77-D53B-3BE6-D9719CC45E8EF4E3.jpg"],shortDescription:"The site of George Washington’s childhood home and the family burial ground.",fullDescription:"This monument celebrates the life and origins of the first U.S. President. While the original house burned in 1779, the site now includes a memorial house representative of the era, the Washington family cemetery, and beautiful views of Pope's Creek and the Potomac River, offering a serene look into 18th-century Tidewater Virginia.",thingsToDo:["Tour the Memorial House","Colonial craft demonstrations","Picnicking by the creek","Visiting the family cemetery"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Dancing Marsh Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A short walk through woods and marshlands with water views."},{name:"Colonial Farm Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.75 miles",description:"Connects the historic structures and farm area."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Visitor Center",info:"Information desk, museum, and film screening area.",phone:"804-224-1732",hours:"9:00 AM - 4:30 PM"},rangerPrograms:["Colonial life talks","Presidential history tours"],campingInfo:"No camping permitted.",wildlife:["Bald eagle","Osprey","White-tailed deer","Blue heron"],bestViewpoints:["Pope's Creek overlook"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"The Memorial Area is open daily from 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.",address:"1732 Popes Creek Rd, Colonial Beach, VA 22443",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=George+Washington+Birthplace+National+Monument",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/gewa/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"Spring when the gardens are blooming",accessibilityInfo:"Grounds are mostly flat and accessible; house has limited accessibility.",travelTips:["Bring bug spray if walking the trails","Picnic supplies recommended","Check the calendar for colonial living history days"],nearbyAttractions:["Westmoreland State Park","Stratford Hall"],designation:"National Monument"},{id:"appomattox-court-house-national-historical-park",name:"Appomattox Court House National Historical Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/6401B157-A6A3-8649-CF81BFB41413C8FA.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/6401B157-A6A3-8649-CF81BFB41413C8FA.jpg"],shortDescription:"The site where General Robert E. Lee surrendered to Lieutenant General Ulysses S. Grant in 1865, effectively ending the Civil War.",fullDescription:"Appomattox Court House is a village frozen in time, representing the end of the American Civil War. The park preserves the McLean House, where the historic meeting took place, as well as the courthouse and surrounding structures, providing a profound space for reflection on national reconciliation.",thingsToDo:["Tour the McLean House","Walking tours of the village","Interpretive living history programs","Park film viewing"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Court House Village Loop",difficulty:"Easy",length:"1.0 mile",description:"An easy walk through the village center and historic buildings."},{name:"Woodland Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"2.5 miles",description:"A forest walk exploring the landscape surrounding the battlefield."}],scenicDrives:[],visitorCenter:{name:"Visitor Center",info:"Located in the historic Clover Hill Tavern building.",phone:"(434) 694-8904",hours:"9:00 AM - 5:00 PM"},rangerPrograms:["Surrender talks","Civil War soldier life demonstrations"],campingInfo:"No camping allowed in the park.",wildlife:["Wild turkey","White-tailed deer","Songbirds","Box turtle"],bestViewpoints:["Village central square"],entranceFees:"Free (no entrance fee)",hours:"The park is open daily from 9-5, with the exception of certain holidays: Thanksgiving Day, December 25, and January 1. The park may have reduced hours (9-3) on December 24.",address:"111 National Park Dr, Appomattox, VA 24522",googleMapsLocation:"https://maps.google.com/?q=Appomattox+Court+House+National+Historical+Park",officialWebsite:"https://www.nps.gov/apco/index.htm",bestTimeToVisit:"April for the anniversary of the surrender",accessibilityInfo:"Village streets are paved or gravel; main buildings have ramp access.",travelTips:["Start at the visitor center for a map","Spend at least 3 hours exploring","Download the NPS app before arrival"],nearbyAttractions:["High Bridge Trail State Park","Museum of the Confederacy"],designation:"National Historical Park"},{id:"cedar-creek-and-belle-grove-national-historical-park",name:"Cedar Creek and Belle Grove National Historical Park",image:"https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/68FB2EF6-E6C0-7996-60940AFF61292B5E.jpg",photoGallery:["https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/68FB2EF6-E6C0-7996-60940AFF61292B5E.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/D0F807F1-0D54-2B98-A94A2D1440CB3DE6.jpg","https://www.nps.gov/common/uploads/structured_data/694406B5-AE14-622B-0F042B7489F116B5.jpg"],shortDescription:"Preserving the site of the 1864 Battle of Cedar Creek in the scenic Shenandoah Valley.",fullDescription:"This park commemorates the Battle of Cedar Creek, a pivotal engagement during the Civil War, and the development of the Shenandoah Valley's agricultural history. It showcases the Belle Grove Manor House, a stunning example of Federal-style architecture.",thingsToDo:["Tour Belle Grove Plantation","Battlefield auto tours","Educational seminars","Hiking trails"],hikingTrails:[{name:"Cedar Creek Battlefield Trail",difficulty:"Moderate",length:"3.0 miles",description:"Trail through historic battle positions and pastures."},{name:"Belle Grove Garden Trail",difficulty:"Easy",length:"0.5 miles",description:"A peaceful walk around the historic manor gardens."}],scenicDrives:[{name:"Battlefield Auto Tour",length:"10 miles",description:"A loop through key points of the 1864 battle."}],visitorCenter:{name:"Visitor Contact Station",info:"Shared facility at the Belle Grove site.",phone:"(540) 490-9569",hours:"10:00 AM - 4:00 PM"},ranger